!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = ESCs (RGd2 containing a Rex1:GFPd2-IRES-Blasticidin reporter (Wray et al., 2011) (gift from Martin Leeb, Vienna) were cultured on plastic coated with gelatin or laminin (Sigma) in N2B27 medium (DMEM/F12 (Life Technologies), Neurobasal (Gibco) supplemented with N2 (homemade) and B-27 Serum-Free Supplement (Gibco), 1mM sodium pyruvate (Gibco), 2mM L-glutamine (Gibco), 0.1 mM 2-mercaptoethanol (Sigma)), and where indicated with 2i for ESC maintenance (3µM CHIR99021 and 1µM PD0325901 (Steward lab, Dresden)) and 4-hydroxytamoxifen (0.1mM, Sigma).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cellular RNA from ESCs, cells 34h after 2i withdrawal, and long-term differentiated cells sorted for Rex1 expression was purified using RNAeasy (Qiagen).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Strand-specific RNA-seq libraries were generated using TruSeq mRNA Library preparation kit (Illumina).
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned using qAlign from the Bioconductor package QuasR (Gaidatzis et al., 2015) (package version 1.16.0) to mouse GRCm38/mm10 genome with default parameters except for splicedAlignment=TRUE, which performs spliced alignments by internally running SpliceMap (Au et al., 2010).
!Sample_data_processing = Alignments were quantified with qCount from the Bioconductor package QuasR (Gaidatzis et al., 2015) (package version 1.16.0) for known UCSC genes obtained from the TxDb.Mmusculus.UCSC.mm10.knownGene package (package version 3.4.0) using default parameters.
!Sample_data_processing = Statistically significantly deregulated genes were identified using edgeR (Robinson et al., 2010) (package version 3.18.0) and these genes were fitted to five separate generalized linear models for different sets of samples. Raw P values were corrected for multiple testing by calculating false discovery rates (FDR) (Benjamini et al., 1995).
!Sample_data_processing = RNA log2 fold changes were used from edgeR. For centred expression, read counts were normalized (dividing by the total number of aligned reads and multiplying with minimal library size, and adding a pseudocount of 8), log2 transformed and differences in log-space of each gene in each sample to its average over all samples was calculated.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Tab-delimited text file containing RPKM values for each Sample (column) and gene (row).
